<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sikandar Adil Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1668–1700</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikandar-lodi">Sikandar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shah">Adil Shah</a> was the last sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>, placed on the throne as a small child in 1672. His reign was marked by feuding among the nobility, the loss of southern conquests to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and local commanders, and growing Mughal pressure. In 1686 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> took Bijapur after a long siege, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Adil Shahi dynasty</a>, and Sikandar died a prisoner in 1700.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sikandar-adil-shah.jpg" alt="Sikandar Adil Shah" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kamal Muhammad; Chand Muhammad · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_House_of_Bijapur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
